  obligation: "THE MAXIMUM IS STILL UNREAD AND A MINIMUM IS NOW READ; THEY ARE OPPOSITE FACTS AND ONLY ONE OF THEM IS THIS TYPE'S. The operator's own NY2 page, www.equinix.com/data-centers/americas-colocation/united-states-colocation/new-york-data-centers/ny2, fetched 2026-09-09 with a full browser user-agent (HTTP 200) and read from RAW HTML with a SUBJECT control rather than a site control, emits a spec table whose row is labelled exactly \"Minimum Cabinet Density\" with the value \"2kVA\", beside a \"Power Distribution\" row reading the facility's volt classes. That is a FLOOR the operator requires a cabinet to commit to, not a CEILING on what a cabinet may draw, so it may not be carried in DensityMarketedMax or DensityMarketedAirOnly - both of those arms are maxima, and putting a minimum in a maximum's field is the same category error as putting kVA in a field named for kilowatts, which this carrier already grew an arm to prevent. It is ALSO apparent power, not real power: kW = kVA x power factor, no power factor is published, so 2kVA does not establish 2kW. Recording it here at full precision so the next reader neither loses it nor mis-files it. RESOLVE by asking the quote for the per-cabinet air-cooled MAXIMUM at NY2 (275 Hartz Way, Secaucus); the minimum below is a commitment floor and is useful for pricing, not for capacity."
